pseudo-Boolean proof version 2.0
* NOT a forgery. This is the ONE shape in which a contradiction derived inside a proofgoal
* scope legitimately discharges the enclosing proof-by-contradiction subproof, and it is the
* guard against over-fixing: it must keep being ACCEPTED, before and after.
*
* `red` with an empty witness is a proof by contradiction, and its goal `#1` is `C|<empty>`,
* which is `C` itself -- so the premise the goal scope adds is `~C`, the very constraint the
* subproof already carries. A contradiction there really is a contradiction from `~C`.
*
* Deleting the `contradiction_proven` promotion outright (rather than restricting it to this
* goal) would reject this proof. That is why the fix records WHICH goal may be promoted rather
* than removing the mechanism.
f 1
red 1 x1 >= 1 ; ; begin
    proofgoal #1
        u >= 1 ;
    end
end
output NONE
conclusion NONE
end pseudo-Boolean proof
